The scope statement at the head of this section covers these too: no
unintended numerical change was observed on the datasets tested, with
F09 and N-01 the two deliberate exceptions described there. On every
sample under bin/ the figures are unchanged, including the Literal
MultiMMC figure in cpp/selftest/refdata/truerand_8bit.res, which the
build still reproduces exactly.

Deliberately not changed, pending NIST: the treatment of a two-symbol
alphabet as binary regardless of the declared sample width (upstream
#253 and PR #256). NIST reads "binary" as a property of the alphabet
rather than of the sample width, and the question of what an explicitly
declared bits_per_symbol should mean for such a dataset is unresolved.
The fork follows upstream's behaviour unchanged.

ea_non_iid, ea_iid and ea_restart are built from this fork; the repairs
listed above and the regression suite cover all three. ea_conditioning,
the only program that links MPFR and GMP, is not built or shipped, and
none of the three that are built links either: verified with otool -L
and nm -u on each binary, and cpp/Makefile still passes COND_LIB only
in the ea_conditioning rule.


